  "summary": "Coconino County Sheriff's Office installed 18 of 20 approved Flock ALPR cameras across the county, including in Oak Creek Canyon, under a $64,627 first-year lease approved by the Board of Supervisors in April. The article details camera locations, a 30-day retention policy, 95 data-sharing agreements (excluding ICE/federal), and contrasts CCSO's rollout with Sedona's recent indefinite pause of its ALPR program.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "CCSO data retention policy is to collect the data and store it for 30 days.",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "CCSO does not have data sharing agreements with Immigration and Customs Enforcement or federal agencies. However, it does have in total 95 data sharing agreements including the Arizona Department of Public Safety, seven county sheriff's offices in Arizona including Yavapai County, sheriffs in Colorado, New Mexico and California.",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "The city of Sedona indefinitely paused its own ALPR program by majority consensus 5-1",
      "paragraph_idx": 19
    }
  ],
